  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nThe forecast hasn't really changed since last forecast package. \nUpper-level ridging is expected to strengthen aloft, yielding \nwidespread triple digit temperatures each afternoon. As per usual, \nthe hottest locations are anticipated to be in the river Valleys \nwhere highs near 105 degrees can be seen along the Pecos River and \nup to 110 degrees in low-lying spots of the Big Bend. Temperatures \nfluctuate a degree or two each day depending on where the ridge axis \nshifts. Additional Heat Advisories will likely be warranted next \nweek as many spots are expected to meet criteria. Rain chances \nremain minimal and most stay dry throughout the extended.\n  \nGreening",
